    <title>b11684</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;details open=&quot;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;tests : catch vanished rows in the fusion baseline (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5871468586&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/30618&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/30618/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/30618&quot;&gt;#30618&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;tests : update the Metal fusion baseline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Re-record the MTL fusion baseline with the current build: 276 rows over 131&lt;br&gt;
dummy models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: pi:llama.cpp/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF (MacBook, M5 Max, 128GB)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;tests : fail test-fusion when a baseline row stops matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The report was built from the counters the run produced, and the baseline was&lt;br&gt;
only ever used as a lookup table, so a fusion that stopped matching produced no&lt;br&gt;
row and was never compared. qwen4exp and mellum lost their fusions this way&lt;br&gt;
while the Fusion / metal job stayed green.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Report a baseline row that the run does not reproduce as a regression. Scope&lt;br&gt;
the pass to the arches that were actually run so --model keeps working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: pi:llama.cpp/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF (MacBook, M5 Max, 128GB)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;pi : never write inline comments unless the user asks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: pi:llama.cpp/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF (MacBook, M5 Max, 128GB)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;tests : keep the mellum dummy model softmax-gated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;mellum reads expert_gating_func from the GGUF since &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5862811787&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/30578&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/30578/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/30578&quot;&gt;#30578&lt;/a&gt;, while the fixture&lt;br&gt;
writes sigmoid for every MoE arch, so the Mellum dummy model stopped building&lt;br&gt;
the softmax MoE routing fusion. Write softmax for mellum, matching the arch&lt;br&gt;
default and the GGUFs that conversion/mellum.py produces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Re-record the MTL baseline: the routing row is back, 277 ok / 0 failed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: pi:llama.cpp/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF (MacBook, M5 Max, 128GB)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;pi : use emoji in the AI stats disclosure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: pi:llama.cpp/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF (MacBook, M5 Max, 128GB)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;pi : list the disclosure model after the hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: pi:llama.cpp/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF (MacBook, M5 Max, 128GB)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;pi : use monochrome symbols in the AI stats disclosure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: pi:llama.cpp/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF (MacBook, M5 Max, 128GB)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;tests : add muse-spark to the Metal fusion baseline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: pi:llama.cpp/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF (MacBook, M5 Max, 128GB)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Website:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://llama.app&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://llama.app&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attestations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
